Falsifies `timetable::proofs::a_time_of_day_skips_nothing`.

The defect: the latest usable minute of the hour is taken instead of the earliest, so every earlier listed minute in that hour is skipped.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(!(listed && x < t))`, with `x` an earlier listed minute in the same hour.

diff --git a/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs b/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs
index e0cdeb116..47f237cbc 100644
--- a/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs
+++ b/crates/timetable/src/recurrence.rs
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@ pub fn next_time(hours: u32, minutes: u64, after: i32) -> Option<u16> {
                 minutes & !((1u64 << (floor + 1)) - 1)
             };
             if usable != 0 {
-                return Some((h * 60 + usable.trailing_zeros()) as u16);
+                return Some((h * 60 + (63 - usable.leading_zeros())) as u16);
             }
         }
         h += 1;
